        "stem": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Haemophilia is a blood condition where bleeding continues for a long period of time after a blood vessel has been damaged.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 20
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A person with haemophilia has a mutation in a gene on the X chromosome, which results in the lack of a blood clotting factor.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 20
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Explain why a man who has haemophilia cannot pass the condition to his male offspring.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "topics": [
          {
