          "heading": null,
          "bullets": [
            "Most candidates were able to correctly define a recessive allele. Many definitions of a codominant allele contained errors or omissions. In codominance neither allele is dominant. The answer that codominant alleles are both expressed ideally needs to be qualified by ‘in a heterozygous individual’. For the recessive allele the description ‘expressed when the dominant allele is not present’ was the most common answer."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
